  </diagram>
  <diagram id="cams-notes" name="Integrity and Scope Notes">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="900" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1160" pageHeight="1122" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
        <mxCell id="n-title" value="Integrity and Scope Notes" style="text;html=1;align=left;fontSize=24;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1e293b;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="40" width="1000" height="36" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n0" value="1.  Admin, Teacher and Student are separate account tables. All three store PasswordHash, FailedLoginAttempts and LockoutEndUtc. No plain Password column exists in any account model." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0f172a;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="100" width="1040" height="66" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n1" value="2.  Only Student has database-enforced unique credentials: unique indexes on StudentNumber and on Username. Admin and Teacher have no unique index on Username, so uniqueness there rests on application logic alone." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0f172a;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="178" width="1040" height="86" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n2" value="3.  CreatedByType and CreatedById record who created a teacher, student or class, and ChangedByType with ChangedById record who changed a workstation status. A teacher can do these things too, so the type column says which table the id belongs to. That is why those connectors are dashed: the database cannot enforce them, and deleting an admin leaves the ids pointing at nobody." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0f172a;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="276" width="1040" height="126" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n3" value="4.  Student.ClassId is the primary class association. ClassStudent carries the explicit roster with its own ClassStudentId primary key and a unique (ClassId, StudentId) pair, which is the constraint that makes class to student a genuine many to many." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0f172a;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="414" width="1040" height="86" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n4" value="5.  Filtered unique indexes permit at most one active LabSession per student, and at most one active LabSession per computer. Because they are filtered they appear as UQ lines rather than UK column marks." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0f172a;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="512" width="1040" height="86" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n5" value="6.  Computer.LaboratoryStation is unique under a NOCASE collation. Computer.AssignedTo holds a student identifier as text, is unique when not null, and is deliberately not a foreign key: assignment integrity is enforced in application code." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0f172a;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="610" width="1040" height="86" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n6" value="7.  A RestrictionRule with IsGlobal set has no teacher owner. A teacher-owned rule carries TeacherId and applies only within that teacher active session scope." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0f172a;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="708" width="1040" height="66" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n7" value="8.  Role, Permission and RolePermissions hold seeded metadata that the Roles and Permissions page displays. They do not drive runtime access control: an account role follows from which account table it lives in, stamped on the login cookie as a claim. No account table links to Role." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0f172a;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="786" width="1040" height="106" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n8" value="9.  Tables omitted here to keep the diagram legible: ActivityEvent, IdleInterval, BrowserMonitoringRecord, MonitoringAlert, Notification, RemoteControlSession, RemoteCommandLog, AuditLog, SystemLog, BlacklistItem, ApplicationCategory, WebsiteCategory and LanConfiguration. They correlate to students, workstations and teachers through scalar identifiers rather than enforced foreign keys. The scope here matches the Chen diagram entity for entity, so the two documents describe the same system at different levels of detail." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=13;fontColor=#0f172a;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="904" width="1040" height="146" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
